questions.prompt:
The contractors group currently has SELECT on the Unity Catalog table main.hr.salaries. To block access, a data engineer runs:

DENY SELECT ON TABLE main.hr.salaries TO `contractors`;

The statement does not work. What is the correct way to remove the group's ability to query the table?

A data engineer applies a row filter to the table orders, whose region_code column is a STRING:

CREATE FUNCTION region_filter(rc INT) RETURNS BOOLEAN
  RETURN IF(is_account_group_member('global_sales'), true, rc IS NULL);
ALTER TABLE orders SET ROW FILTER region_filter ON (region_code);

The session has spark.sql.ansi.enabled = false. Users outside global_sales should see only rows where region_code is NULL, but they see every row and no error is raised. What is the cause, and how should it be fixed?

A data engineer who is NOT the owner of the existing table prod.sales.orders must run:

ALTER TABLE prod.sales.orders SET ROW FILTER prod.sec.region_filter ON (region);

The engineer already has USE CATALOG on prod and USE SCHEMA on prod.sales and prod.sec. The statement does not change the table schema. Which TWO additional privilege requirements must be met? (Select TWO)
